+/// Enable or disable continuous collision for this body. It is on by default, and the world's setting
+/// still applies. With it off the body is never swept, so it can pass through thin static shapes
+/// when it moves further in a step than its speculative margin. A body made of many small shapes
+/// is swept shape by shape whenever its smallest shape moves fast enough, which can cost more
+/// than the rest of the step.
+B3_API void b3Body_EnableContinuous( b3BodyId bodyId, bool flag );
+
+/// Is continuous collision enabled for this body?
+B3_API bool b3Body_IsContinuousEnabled( b3BodyId bodyId );
+
 /// Allow this body to rotate fast. Useful for axially symmetric bodies, such as vehicle wheels.
 /// Normally rotation speed is clamped to improve CCD. However, this clamping is unnecessary for
 /// bodies that only rotate fast around an axis of symmetry.
